invariant: INV-13
file: io.c
catches: rec_loop_test
reason: a record-mode ch_read reports CH_RECORD_AGAIN for a recv that
  stops inside a record, after its first byte. The bytes already read are
  lost and the session stays live, so the caller can retry past a broken
  stream; INV-13 admits the result only at a record boundary.

--- old
    int rc = read_exact(cfg, buf + got, REC_HDR - (size_t)got);
#else
--- new
    int rc = read_exact(cfg, buf + got, REC_HDR - (size_t)got);
    if (rc == CH_EIO) {
        return CH_RECORD_AGAIN;
    }
#else
